  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Beira Land Administration Systems (BLAS) phase II (2022-2027)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is a follow-up of the BLAS 1 project and addresses Beira&apos;s severe urban challenges, including climate vulnerability, rapid population growth, expanding informal settlements, and limited municipal resources. The project is anchored in a Theory of Change. It aims to strengthen the Municipality of Beira (CMB) so it can deliver more effective, responsive, and resilient services to citizens.The project focuses on three outcomes. &#x2022;	Outcome 1: improves the effectiveness, efficiency, and sustainability of land administration by streamlining and digitising processes, strengthening links between land registration and taxation, upgrading IT systems, and developing a financial sustainability strategy for the cadastre. This will reduce processing times, improve service delivery, and increase municipal revenues.&#x2022;	Outcome 2 promotes more orderly urban planning and land allocation, particularly in expansion areas and informal neighbourhoods. It supports better use of the Land Administration System, inclusive planning processes, pilot projects with communities, and capacity building in urban planning and monitoring, with attention to flood risk and living conditions.&#x2022;	Outcome 3 strengthens CMB&apos;s leadership, coordination, communication, and execution capacity. This includes establishing donor coordination led by CMB, improving engagement with civil society and the private sector, enhancing external communication, and reinforcing internal leadership and the Mayor&apos;s office.Together, these interventions contribute to a more resilient, well-governed Beira aligned with broader Netherlands-Beira cooperation goals.</narrative>
  </description>
